WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.926
A NETFLIX SERIES

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:22.689
KOTARO LIVES ALONE

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:14.365
GOURMET?!/DODGER KOTARO

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:16.367
Yes?

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.204
Pleased to meet you.

00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:23.124
I am Kotaro Sato, of the Star Class
at Shimizu Kindergarten.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:26.836
Thank you kindly for inviting me today.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.506
Are you Sir Kakeru's mother?

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:32.008
Please accept this token of thanks.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.511
Well, thank you for your kindness.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.806
But, I'm not Kakeru's mother.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.059
Kotaro! You're here.

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:42.894
Come in quickly!

00:01:42.977 --> 00:01:44.813
Yes. Please pardon me.

00:01:46.856 --> 00:01:47.857
What are you doing?

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.485
Let Ms. Yoshida do that and come on in.

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:55.615
You are Ms. Yoshida?

00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:58.243
I'm the housekeeper.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:01.246
Since Kakeru's parents both work.

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:03.790
Ms. Yoshida, bring out the snacks.

00:02:03.873 --> 00:02:05.834
Also, put away the toys too.

00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:06.918
Sure!

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.380
KAKERU'S ROOM

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:12.340
Ta-da!

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:14.926
This is the legendary…

00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:18.555
It's wonderful… very wonderful.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.683
I didn't know you liked Tonosaman too!

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.728
Oh, no!

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.939
Ms. Yoshida, bring a towel!

00:02:28.022 --> 00:02:28.857
Okay!

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.820
Could you bring another glass of juice?

00:02:33.903 --> 00:02:34.863
Sure.

00:02:34.946 --> 00:02:37.448
Also, charge the video game.

00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:38.366
Sure.

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:41.828
A FEW DAYS LATER

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:44.414
How long are we gonna be walking?

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.458
I'm already tired,
I don't wanna walk anymore.

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:48.877
This distance is nothing.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.045
Then, pull me by my hands.

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:53.715
No way. You need to walk on your own.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.051
Well, we've reached our goal.

00:02:57.927 --> 00:03:00.305
What will we do in a place like this?

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:03.224
I'll have you fish for crayfish now.

00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:05.768
What? I've never fished before!

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:09.480
We will make rods
with these chopsticks and string.

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:12.817
What? I can't do that.
Kotaro, you do it.

00:03:13.401 --> 00:03:15.528
No. You need to do it yourself.

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:17.155
Aww…

00:03:22.493 --> 00:03:24.078
Now is the time! Pull it up!

00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:30.543
What do I do?

00:03:30.627 --> 00:03:33.463
Calm down. Grab the crayfish's back.

00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:37.467
Ow!

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.676
Kotaro, help me!

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.719
Sir Kakeru!

00:03:40.303 --> 00:03:42.680
You should not rely on people so easily!

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.977
This is not bad for your first time.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.771
What do we do with these?

00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:50.855
Eat them, of course.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:53.149
What? I don't want to eat these!

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:56.527
Do you not know?
These are a delicacy in Europe.

00:03:56.611 --> 00:03:59.447
They are also rich in protein,
essential for growth.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.449
Why do you know that?

00:04:02.992 --> 00:04:04.369
I have been through a lot.

00:04:08.456 --> 00:04:11.709
We need them to spit out the mud
before eating them…

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.379
But today,

00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:16.714
I have some pre-washed ones in here.

00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:18.633
This feels like a cooking show.

00:04:18.716 --> 00:04:21.803
Since you are new to crayfish, Sir Kakeru,

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:24.264
it would be good to try it
in miso soup first.

00:04:24.347 --> 00:04:26.474
We aren't going to eat it as is?

00:04:27.058 --> 00:04:29.811
You must absolutely not eat it raw.

00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:32.021
Okay. Got it.

00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:38.236
But couldn't we just buy something,
instead of eating them?

00:04:38.319 --> 00:04:41.572
We could just have Mom or Ms. Yoshida
make us something to eat.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.159
You are lacking a sense of urgency.

00:04:45.743 --> 00:04:48.997
Us children are weak beings.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.916
When you lack money,
or have no father or mother,

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.461
or Ms. Yoshida or any adult,
what will you do?

00:04:57.755 --> 00:04:58.881
I'd hate that!

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.967
Not having Mama and them would be awful!

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.136
I'd be in trouble.

00:05:05.221 --> 00:05:06.180
In these times!

00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:09.309
You need to be able to protect yourself!

00:05:13.604 --> 00:05:15.982
That's why we fished for crayfish!

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:20.028
Speaking of which,

00:05:20.111 --> 00:05:22.655
no one's at your house, Kotaro.

00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:24.657
Tell me if you get lonely!

00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:26.617
I'll go catch some crayfish for you!

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:33.124
I would be grateful for that.

00:05:41.299 --> 00:05:43.176
What's with the tissues in your nose?

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.678
It is not a big deal.

00:05:45.762 --> 00:05:48.473
We were playing dodgeball today…

00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:50.975
And the ball hit Kotaro's face.

00:05:51.642 --> 00:05:53.353
That caused the nosebleed.

00:05:53.978 --> 00:05:56.022
Therefore, Sir Karino,

00:05:56.105 --> 00:05:57.815
I have a favor to ask of you.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:05:59.692
MIDORI FOREST PARK

00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:01.235
Okay, Sir Karino.

00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:05.073
Please guide me to master the art
of catching the ball.

00:06:05.156 --> 00:06:06.491
Why do I have to…

00:06:07.325 --> 00:06:08.993
Alright, I'll throw it.

00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:10.703
Yes. Come at me.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.254
Sir Karino,

00:06:20.338 --> 00:06:22.382
you do not need to go easy on me.

00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:24.258
No. Are you sure?

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:29.389
What now?

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:31.599
Should we stop?

00:06:31.682 --> 00:06:34.185
Is there any secret to this?

00:06:34.268 --> 00:06:35.103
What?

00:06:35.603 --> 00:06:37.146
Well, now that you mention it,

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.856
the ball is a word!

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:42.944
My baseball coach used to say catching
a ball is like having a conversation.

00:06:44.445 --> 00:06:46.614
Not sure if that's a secret.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.033
Let's try to practice throwing.

00:06:49.117 --> 00:06:49.951
It is dodgeball.

00:06:50.952 --> 00:06:52.203
What's wrong?

00:06:55.498 --> 00:06:57.667
What was that?

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:00.002
I will not throw it.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:01.379
My specialty is catching.

00:07:02.046 --> 00:07:03.172
I don't get it at all…

00:07:04.507 --> 00:07:05.633
Here I go!

00:07:09.137 --> 00:07:12.557
Kotaro got hit in the face again!
The face is a safe area!

00:07:23.151 --> 00:07:26.487
Maybe Kotaro doesn't understand
the rules of dodgeball?

00:07:31.492 --> 00:07:32.869
I am disappointed…

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:34.871
I couldn't catch a single throw.

00:07:35.413 --> 00:07:38.541
I guess we have no choice.
I'll train you again today.

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.087
COMPLETE DEFEAT

00:07:43.171 --> 00:07:44.297
Sorry…

00:07:44.839 --> 00:07:46.132
No, don't worry about it.

00:07:46.757 --> 00:07:47.758
I mean,

00:07:48.259 --> 00:07:50.428
if you can't catch the ball,
can't you run?

00:07:50.511 --> 00:07:51.637
That's not acceptable.

00:07:51.721 --> 00:07:52.555
Huh?

00:07:53.598 --> 00:07:57.518
If I dodge a ball a friend threw,
it means I ignored them.

00:07:58.102 --> 00:07:58.978
Huh?

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.780
Didn't you say,
to think of the ball as a word?

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.160
Isn't it painful
to throw a ball at someone

00:08:14.243 --> 00:08:16.287
who has no intention of catching it?

00:08:23.044 --> 00:08:24.045
It may be painful.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.798
No, it may have been painful,

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:29.759
but if you don't throw the ball,

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.260
no one will understand you.

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:32.803
And,

00:08:33.304 --> 00:08:34.722
I don't know your situation,

00:08:35.306 --> 00:08:36.933
but if you threw the ball a bit,

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:40.061
I'm sure it was received,
even if it wasn't returned.

00:08:40.144 --> 00:08:41.145
That's what I think.

00:08:50.655 --> 00:08:52.198
Alright, here I go!

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:56.410
Kotaro caught it!

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:58.079
I caught it…

00:08:58.704 --> 00:09:00.331
Run away!

00:09:05.586 --> 00:09:07.964
Your throw's a piece of cake, Kotaro!

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:09.507
I can catch it many times!

00:09:11.008 --> 00:09:11.884
Yes.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:14.345
It was a great catch!

00:09:14.428 --> 00:09:16.764
Why are you so happy about it?

00:09:16.847 --> 00:09:19.183
Whose side are you on, Kotaro?

00:09:19.267 --> 00:09:21.477
I am on everyone's side!

00:09:26.774 --> 00:09:28.317
WHAT IS A BIRTHDAY?/LET'S RUN AWAY

00:09:28.401 --> 00:09:29.443
Sir Hanbe.

00:09:29.527 --> 00:09:32.071
When is your birthday?

00:09:32.154 --> 00:09:35.032
How are we going to find out
a stray cat's birthday?

00:09:35.116 --> 00:09:38.536
Forget that, what's with
the crown on your head?

00:09:38.619 --> 00:09:41.539
A birthday party at kindergarten.

00:09:41.622 --> 00:09:43.165
I received it there.

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:44.208
I see…

00:09:45.835 --> 00:09:47.878
It's your birthday this month?

00:09:48.504 --> 00:09:50.006
Yes. That is the case.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:51.966
It's your birthday, Kotaro?!

00:09:52.049 --> 00:09:54.594
What? It's Kotaro's birthday?!

00:09:54.677 --> 00:09:57.179
Alright, then let's have a birthday party!

00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:58.306
Let's do it!

00:09:58.389 --> 00:10:01.809
I already had a birthday party
at kindergarten.

00:10:01.892 --> 00:10:04.395
Come on, what are you saying, Kotaro?

00:10:04.478 --> 00:10:07.189
You can celebrate
as many times as you want!

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:09.692
A birthday party is a celebration?

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:15.698
Yes, it's a party to celebrate
and be thankful for being born.

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:17.366
I see.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:21.662
I thought a birthday party was just
an event to blow out candles on a cake.

00:10:21.746 --> 00:10:23.998
Well, you're not wrong.

00:10:24.749 --> 00:10:25.916
I see now.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:30.254
I didn't know me being born
was a good thing.

00:10:36.552 --> 00:10:38.679
If that's what a birthday party is,

00:10:38.763 --> 00:10:40.640
we need to prepare.

00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:49.732
Did you know?

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:54.904
You can train your lung capacity
by breathing into a plastic bottle.

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:58.074
I knew that, but why are you suddenly
talking about lung capacity?

00:10:58.157 --> 00:11:01.827
To blow out the candles
in one breath, of course.

00:11:01.911 --> 00:11:04.538
If you can do that,
something good will happen.

00:11:04.622 --> 00:11:05.456
Really?

00:11:06.123 --> 00:11:08.292
But with candles for someone your age,

00:11:08.376 --> 00:11:10.503
- it's easy--
- there's also the song.

00:11:14.799 --> 00:11:17.176
Hey, listen, Tone-Deaf.

00:11:17.259 --> 00:11:19.261
SIT-UPS

00:11:19.345 --> 00:11:21.222
BREATH HOLDING

00:11:21.305 --> 00:11:23.182
RUNNING

00:11:23.265 --> 00:11:25.142
IMAGE TRAINING

00:11:25.226 --> 00:11:26.769
SHIMIZU CONVENIENCE STORE

00:11:26.852 --> 00:11:27.728
Yes.

00:11:27.812 --> 00:11:29.689
Will this be enough?

00:11:29.772 --> 00:11:32.066
BIRTHDAY CANDLES
5 PER PACK

00:11:32.149 --> 00:11:33.067
BIRTHDAY DAY

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:34.402
Ta-da!

00:11:34.485 --> 00:11:36.987
Wow. That is incredible.

00:11:37.071 --> 00:11:39.365
Okay, we need to put on the candles.

00:11:39.448 --> 00:11:41.325
- Do we have matches?
- We do.

00:11:41.409 --> 00:11:43.869
Also, I brought these for you two.

00:11:43.953 --> 00:11:44.954
Put them on!

00:11:45.037 --> 00:11:47.081
Oh, good idea.

00:11:48.207 --> 00:11:49.709
They look good on you!

00:11:49.792 --> 00:11:51.669
Alright, let's try this again…

00:11:53.212 --> 00:11:54.046
He's not here?

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:55.589
The cake's gone too…

00:11:59.593 --> 00:12:01.554
"I apologize profusely,

00:12:01.637 --> 00:12:03.639
but I'm borrowing the cake for a while…"

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.350
Borrowing the cake?

00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:11.313
I need to celebrate
for my important friends too!

00:12:13.441 --> 00:12:17.445
Are you ready? Today, I am giving you
a surprise birthday party.

00:12:19.363 --> 00:12:21.657
Since I don't know how old you guys are,

00:12:21.741 --> 00:12:23.617
I brought a lot of candles.

00:12:24.326 --> 00:12:26.162
Okay, let us start.

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:31.167
Apologies,
there is only one cake for all of you.

00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:42.678
Sir Hanbe, Sir Kanbe

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:44.680
Sir Sakon, Sir Kojuro

00:12:53.355 --> 00:12:55.316
I am out of oxygen.

00:12:58.319 --> 00:13:01.071
Today is all of your birthdays.

00:13:01.739 --> 00:13:05.326
It is a celebration
because I am glad all of you were born!

00:13:09.914 --> 00:13:12.082
Yes. I see.

00:13:12.666 --> 00:13:14.919
Nothing is better than
you guys being happy!

00:13:18.798 --> 00:13:21.509
The main guest is late.

00:13:25.471 --> 00:13:26.639
Kotaro!

00:13:26.722 --> 00:13:28.599
Run away with me!

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:30.684
Run away?

00:13:32.019 --> 00:13:34.104
I can't take it anymore!

00:13:34.188 --> 00:13:37.233
My mom is on my case every day!

00:13:37.316 --> 00:13:41.570
"Wake up!" "Did you wash your hands?"
and "Did you flush the toilet?"

00:13:42.238 --> 00:13:43.948
So, I'm running away!

00:13:44.031 --> 00:13:45.491
Well, Sir Takuya,

00:13:46.158 --> 00:13:48.661
what will we really do when we run away?

00:13:49.245 --> 00:13:50.079
Huh?

00:13:52.122 --> 00:13:54.166
For now, we'll go to a faraway place!

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.835
We'll also be bad kids!

00:13:56.377 --> 00:13:58.504
We'll do bad things and cause trouble!

00:13:58.587 --> 00:14:01.924
Sir Takuya,
you need to treasure your family.

00:14:02.007 --> 00:14:03.467
You don't get it.

00:14:03.551 --> 00:14:07.137
We're running away and being bad
so they realize how important we are!

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:09.473
I see.

00:14:10.182 --> 00:14:12.685
Okay, it's 740 yen.

00:14:13.269 --> 00:14:14.895
What do you think, Kotaro?

00:14:14.979 --> 00:14:17.940
Buy more than 150 yen of snacks at once.

00:14:18.023 --> 00:14:19.358
Isn't that bad?!

00:14:23.362 --> 00:14:25.197
I will pay for it.

00:14:27.157 --> 00:14:30.786
- What? You don't have a 150 yen rule?!
- No.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:33.747
How nice. You can eat
as many snacks as you like.

00:14:33.831 --> 00:14:36.750
You also have so much money. I'm jealous.

00:14:37.918 --> 00:14:38.878
Sir Takuya.

00:14:38.961 --> 00:14:42.214
We've only been
to the local convenience store and park.

00:14:42.298 --> 00:14:44.717
Didn't you say we were going far away?

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:48.679
I don't really know how to go far away.

00:14:49.305 --> 00:14:51.765
Don't we ride a train or something?

00:14:51.849 --> 00:14:53.058
That's no good, Kotaro.

00:14:53.142 --> 00:14:56.770
Mom said it's not okay for kids
to ride a train by themselves.

00:14:57.313 --> 00:14:59.148
What happened to being bad?

00:15:00.941 --> 00:15:02.860
Look at us, playing at night.

00:15:02.943 --> 00:15:04.111
We're bad kids.

00:15:04.653 --> 00:15:06.864
Is it bad to play at night?

00:15:06.947 --> 00:15:10.451
So, playing at night isn't off-limits
at your house either?

00:15:10.534 --> 00:15:12.286
I have never been told that.

00:15:12.369 --> 00:15:15.497
Man, I'm really jealous of you.

00:15:17.166 --> 00:15:18.000
Sir Takuya,

00:15:19.001 --> 00:15:20.002
I…

00:15:20.961 --> 00:15:23.923
am not jealous of myself.

00:15:24.006 --> 00:15:26.550
You don't get it, Kotaro.

00:15:26.634 --> 00:15:29.887
You don't know how lucky you are.

00:15:30.888 --> 00:15:32.556
Anyways, it's dark…

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.767
I don't want
to sleep in the park at night.

00:15:35.351 --> 00:15:37.937
In that case, why not come to my place?

00:15:39.647 --> 00:15:41.899
Sorry to bother you, Kotaro.

00:15:41.982 --> 00:15:44.318
I was afraid of running away by myself.

00:15:44.818 --> 00:15:45.861
But hey,

00:15:45.945 --> 00:15:48.030
since you were out until this time,

00:15:48.113 --> 00:15:50.574
your mom and dad must be worried too.

00:15:51.158 --> 00:15:52.201
Worried?

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:56.372
Yeah, the purpose of running away
was to worry mom and dad!

00:15:56.455 --> 00:16:01.543
Thanks to me, they'll realize
how important you are.

00:16:06.715 --> 00:16:07.549
Kotaro,

00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:09.885
where are your mom and dad?

00:16:10.886 --> 00:16:14.098
My parents are not at home because
they are at ninja training.

00:16:14.765 --> 00:16:18.102
Therefore, there is no one waiting here
to worry about me.

00:16:22.064 --> 00:16:23.565
Sorry, Kotaro.

00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:25.275
I'm gonna go home after all.

00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:27.611
I'm sorry, Kotaro!

00:16:34.743 --> 00:16:36.203
"Worry them"…

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:38.664
I see.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.626
It is not possible for me to run away.

00:16:45.295 --> 00:16:46.672
Hey, you!

00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:49.299
Where were you?
This is when we go to the bathhouse!

00:16:49.383 --> 00:16:52.302
I went to the bathhouse
three times looking for you!

00:16:53.053 --> 00:16:54.263
Sir Karino…

00:16:55.848 --> 00:16:58.392
Sorry! Sorry for worrying you!

00:16:58.976 --> 00:17:00.894
He's being sincere for some reason.

00:17:00.978 --> 00:17:03.188
Well, as long as you understand.

00:17:03.814 --> 00:17:05.149
But, Sir Karino,

00:17:05.232 --> 00:17:08.318
I made no promise to go to
the bathhouse with you to begin with--

00:17:08.402 --> 00:17:09.570
Enough!

00:17:12.406 --> 00:17:15.034
GET DRUNK AND DANCE/SUMMER FESTIVAL

00:17:15.117 --> 00:17:17.077
This is magic hand power!

00:17:17.619 --> 00:17:19.538
That's amazing, Kotaro!

00:17:19.621 --> 00:17:22.041
You really do have superpowers!

00:17:23.083 --> 00:17:27.212
Well then, it's about time.
Here's your money for this week!

00:17:27.796 --> 00:17:29.673
Thank you for this every week.

00:17:29.757 --> 00:17:31.925
Here is my gift for you as well.

00:17:37.181 --> 00:17:39.141
Is it a donation from a kind person?

00:17:39.224 --> 00:17:40.893
Yes! It is!

00:17:42.019 --> 00:17:43.062
I see…

00:17:48.525 --> 00:17:50.694
I got through it safely this time too.

00:17:51.195 --> 00:17:52.696
ONE WEEK LATER

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:57.326
Tonosaman

00:17:57.993 --> 00:18:00.412
Lady Kobayashi, are you enjoying this?

00:18:00.496 --> 00:18:03.874
Yes! Your wonderful voice
is always the best!

00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:06.835
Lady Kobayashi.

00:18:06.919 --> 00:18:10.589
You always look stiff and nervous.

00:18:11.215 --> 00:18:12.674
What do you mean?

00:18:13.425 --> 00:18:16.053
I would like you to relax.

00:18:16.637 --> 00:18:19.098
I want to speak with the real you.

00:18:20.224 --> 00:18:22.851
Is there something you cannot say to me?

00:18:23.519 --> 00:18:25.729
That's not the case!

00:18:25.813 --> 00:18:27.773
I'm always like this.

00:18:28.273 --> 00:18:30.567
No. He can't find out…

00:18:31.235 --> 00:18:34.655
I can't let him know that the money
is from his mother's insurance,

00:18:34.738 --> 00:18:36.031
no matter what!

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:41.036
I wonder who it is…

00:18:43.747 --> 00:18:46.250
This is a package
for your neighbor, Mr. Karino.

00:18:46.333 --> 00:18:49.002
Since he's not at home,
may I leave it with you?

00:18:49.086 --> 00:18:52.089
So, I just need to hand it to Sir Karino
once he gets home?

00:18:52.172 --> 00:18:53.966
Yes, thank you.

00:18:57.886 --> 00:18:58.720
This is…

00:19:00.764 --> 00:19:03.308
Lady Kobayashi, how about a drink?

00:19:03.392 --> 00:19:05.144
What? Beer?!

00:19:05.227 --> 00:19:08.105
Here, please help yourself.

00:19:08.188 --> 00:19:10.899
The golden ratio of 7:3!

00:19:10.983 --> 00:19:13.569
In any case, why do you have beer?!

00:19:13.652 --> 00:19:15.946
Do not worry about trivial things.

00:19:16.029 --> 00:19:17.281
What? But…

00:19:22.077 --> 00:19:23.704
Look at this!

00:19:23.787 --> 00:19:24.746
A masterpiece!

00:19:26.248 --> 00:19:29.126
I'm laughing so much,
my stomach, no, my face hurts!

00:19:34.882 --> 00:19:36.758
Okay! It's empty.

00:19:36.842 --> 00:19:39.511
Man, those superpowers earlier?

00:19:39.595 --> 00:19:41.263
They really startled me!

00:19:41.346 --> 00:19:44.057
You do so many things
even though you're a kindergartner.

00:19:44.141 --> 00:19:47.060
I thought you were an alien!

00:19:47.144 --> 00:19:50.105
But if you look at
the spoon closely, it's a toy,

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:52.316
and despite your talents,
you're tone-deaf!

00:19:54.067 --> 00:19:58.697
Yes. I am happy to see
your liberated self today.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:01.533
Yay! Naked dance!

00:20:01.617 --> 00:20:03.035
So, Ms. Kobayashi…

00:20:03.827 --> 00:20:06.914
is the money truly from a kind person?

00:20:23.305 --> 00:20:25.974
Do you really want to know?

00:20:27.643 --> 00:20:29.061
That money is…

00:20:31.396 --> 00:20:35.275
really a donation from a kind person!

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:39.655
Really, it really is.

00:20:40.405 --> 00:20:41.240
I am sorry.

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.533
That's really the truth.

00:20:44.034 --> 00:20:46.453
Sorry,.

00:20:47.454 --> 00:20:49.957
- Really.
- It's okay, Lady Kobayashi.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:51.833
I am sorry.

00:20:51.917 --> 00:20:56.463
Sorry…

00:21:08.016 --> 00:21:10.269
For considering my feelings,

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:12.646
you have my thanks.

00:21:15.357 --> 00:21:17.943
Hey. I came to get my beer. Huh?

00:21:18.735 --> 00:21:20.404
It's oil-based magic marker.

00:21:20.487 --> 00:21:22.739
Alcohol is terrifying…

00:21:22.823 --> 00:21:25.534
Who is that woman?! Why is she naked?

00:21:25.617 --> 00:21:29.037
Lady Kobayashi. I look forward to
seeing you again next week.

00:21:32.249 --> 00:21:34.710
That was the first guardian meeting.

00:21:35.294 --> 00:21:37.170
My first impression of him

00:21:37.254 --> 00:21:39.715
was really terrible.

00:21:42.426 --> 00:21:45.554
He's Kotaro Sato's guardian…

00:21:46.138 --> 00:21:48.390
Even in a guardian
and parent fellowship meeting,

00:21:48.473 --> 00:21:50.892
a lack of motivation oozed from his body,

00:21:50.976 --> 00:21:53.812
and there was no sign
he wanted to bond with the others.

00:21:56.106 --> 00:21:57.149
I'm so sleepy.

00:21:57.232 --> 00:21:58.984
Are you busy with your manga?

00:22:00.152 --> 00:22:00.986
Hey.

00:22:01.528 --> 00:22:05.407
Wasn't Kotaro's guardian with some guy
that looked like a yakuza

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:08.035
and a hostess at the entrance ceremony?

00:22:08.118 --> 00:22:10.829
Yeah, they were there!
He was in a sweatsuit then too.

00:22:10.912 --> 00:22:12.873
He's not even the father, right?

00:22:12.956 --> 00:22:15.917
Kotaro's family sounds complicated…

00:22:16.543 --> 00:22:17.711
He's not his real kid.

00:22:17.794 --> 00:22:20.672
That's why he's so unmotivated, right?

00:22:20.756 --> 00:22:22.674
Poor Kotaro.

00:22:22.758 --> 00:22:24.468
Yeah, seriously.

00:22:25.135 --> 00:22:27.220
I'm worried about the future…

00:22:28.221 --> 00:22:30.640
A FEW MONTHS LATER

00:22:30.724 --> 00:22:33.935
In this meeting, the board
would like to make a request

00:22:34.019 --> 00:22:38.357
regarding the summer festival that will
take place soon at Shimizu Kindergarten.

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.901
We'd like the teachers to help

00:22:40.984 --> 00:22:43.236
with booths and hosting,

00:22:43.820 --> 00:22:46.323
but we know we don't have enough people.

00:22:46.406 --> 00:22:51.286
Therefore, we'd like to ask for help,
the day before and of the festival.

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:54.039
No one's making eye contact with me.

00:22:54.831 --> 00:22:58.877
Of course, no one wants to go
out of their way to do this.

00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:02.089
They're overwhelmed,
taking care of kids and doing chores.

00:23:02.172 --> 00:23:03.048
So am I.

00:23:05.258 --> 00:23:07.135
Then, we can rethink the booths--

00:23:07.219 --> 00:23:09.846
I don't mind doing it.

00:23:10.597 --> 00:23:12.265
- Huh?!

00:23:12.849 --> 00:23:15.185
It says to have several people
from this group,

00:23:15.852 --> 00:23:18.563
but I can take care of it myself.

00:23:18.647 --> 00:23:20.524
Huh?!

00:23:20.607 --> 00:23:24.403
Will you be okay
taking care of it by yourself?

00:23:24.486 --> 00:23:27.155
Well, I think it'll work out.

00:23:27.239 --> 00:23:28.490
Thank you very much!

00:23:28.573 --> 00:23:31.326
I think the others
are relieved to hear that.

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:34.454
I'm also sure the kids will be happy!

00:23:34.538 --> 00:23:35.747
It's no big deal…

00:23:36.581 --> 00:23:39.584
I thought this was a guardian's role, so…

00:23:39.668 --> 00:23:40.836
Oh…

00:23:47.926 --> 00:23:49.886
How about some cotton candy?

00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:51.596
What is this?

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:55.058
Lady Mizuki! Sir Tamaru!

00:23:55.142 --> 00:23:57.018
The clerk at the convenience store,

00:23:57.102 --> 00:23:59.604
and even Sir Karino's editor!

00:23:59.688 --> 00:24:02.774
That's amazing, Kotaro.
They're all people you know!

00:24:02.858 --> 00:24:03.692
Yes!

00:24:04.276 --> 00:24:06.153
So that's what he meant.

00:24:08.947 --> 00:24:10.282
Mr. Karino.

00:24:10.365 --> 00:24:13.452
Thank you for your help. This is for you.

00:24:13.535 --> 00:24:14.619
Oh, thank you.

00:24:17.581 --> 00:24:21.168
To be frank, when you volunteered,

00:24:21.251 --> 00:24:22.836
I was very surprised.

00:24:23.628 --> 00:24:24.671
I'm sorry.

00:24:25.255 --> 00:24:28.258
I'm really regretting
the decision I made then.

00:24:29.509 --> 00:24:31.261
It's a lot of work, isn't it?

00:24:34.347 --> 00:24:35.474
But…

00:24:36.433 --> 00:24:38.143
he seems happy, I'm so glad.

00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:40.979
I see all of you

00:24:41.521 --> 00:24:46.401
think about Kotaro's happiness first
before you take action.

00:24:47.068 --> 00:24:48.778
As a parent with a young child,

00:24:48.862 --> 00:24:51.198
I was a little moved by this.

00:24:51.698 --> 00:24:52.532
But…

00:24:53.450 --> 00:24:55.952
in the end, we're not his parents.

00:24:56.661 --> 00:24:59.372
Wouldn't it have been better
if he had parents?

00:25:01.374 --> 00:25:04.252
Sir Karino! Thank you for today!

00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:07.672
It's fine. Kids don't need to
worry about that.

00:25:07.756 --> 00:25:09.007
Just go out and have fun!

00:25:09.090 --> 00:25:09.925
Yes!

00:25:13.011 --> 00:25:15.222
I didn't know
what the situation was exactly…

00:25:16.556 --> 00:25:19.142
but, I sort of thought it would be great

00:25:19.851 --> 00:25:21.186
if he was Kotaro's father.
